## Usage

```bash
terraform init

# dev
terraform workspace new dev || terraform workspace select dev
terraform plan  -var-file=dev.tfvars
terraform apply -var-file=dev.tfvars

# prod — separate state key, separate plan/apply
terraform workspace select prod
terraform plan  -var-file=prod.tfvars
terraform apply -var-file=prod.tfvars
```

### Overriding the DB password from an encrypted source

The default path generates the password in Terraform and stores it in Secrets Manager. If you must supply your own:

```bash
sops -d secrets/prod.enc.tfvars > /dev/shm/prod-secrets.tfvars
terraform apply -var-file=prod.tfvars -var-file=/dev/shm/prod-secrets.tfvars
shred -u /dev/shm/prod-secrets.tfvars
```

Only `secrets/prod.enc.tfvars` (ciphertext) is committed. Add to `.gitignore`:

```
*.auto.tfvars
secrets/*.tfvars
!secrets/*.enc.tfvars
```

