## Acceptance criteria mapping

| # | Criterion | Implementation |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Bucket versioned, encrypted, private | `aws_s3_bucket_versioning` Enabled; SSE AES-256 (dev) / KMS + bucket keys (prod); full `public_access_block` + `BucketOwnerEnforced` + TLS-only bucket policy |
| 2 | RDS protected | `deletion_protection = true` (unconditional), `backup_retention_period >= 7` (validated), `publicly_accessible = false`, `storage_encrypted = true`, `rds.force_ssl = 1` |
| 3 | Secret never plaintext in Git | Generated by `random_password`, written only to KMS-encrypted Secrets Manager; state in encrypted S3 backend; optional SOPS-decrypted tfvars kept out of Git |
| 4 | Least privilege, no prod wildcards | Explicit action lists scoped to one bucket ARN + one secret ARN; KMS scoped by `kms:ViaService`; IAM user blocked in prod by precondition |
| 5 | Cluster sizing | Out of scope for this module; `oidc_provider_arn`/`_url` inputs make it composable with the EKS module |
| 6 | HTTPS | Out of scope; module enforces TLS at the data layer (S3 `SecureTransport` deny, `force_ssl`) |
| 7 | Environment isolation | Workspace-keyed backend (`env:/<ws>/...`), per-env tfvars, workspace↔`environment` consistency precondition |
